# About Me Klairs — Project Rules

Personal portfolio site for Klairs. **Maintenance mode: prefer small, low-risk
changes.**

## Read first

- [`CLAUDE.md`](../../CLAUDE.md) — top-level instructions.
- [`docs/ai/README.md`](../../docs/ai/README.md) — doc map / entry point.
- [`docs/ai/ARCHITECTURE.md`](../../docs/ai/ARCHITECTURE.md) — how the app is built.
- [`docs/ai/TECH_DEBT.md`](../../docs/ai/TECH_DEBT.md) — traps to know before editing.

## Stack

Vite 5 · React 18 · TypeScript 5 · Tailwind CSS 3 · react-router-dom 7 ·
deployed on Vercel. Icons: `lucide-react` only. Package manager: npm.

## Conventions

- **Content lives in `src/data/*.ts`**, not hardcoded in page components. Edit
  data there; `src/pages/*` render it (e.g. `CaseStudyPage` uses `getCaseStudy`).
- **i18n:** user-facing strings for sub-pages go through `src/data/translations.ts`
  and are read via `useLanguage()` from `src/lib/i18n.tsx`.
- **Styling:** match what a file already uses (Tailwind utilities, custom classes
  in `src/index.css`, or inline styles in `App.tsx`). Use the design tokens from
  `tailwind.config.js` (`ivory`, `navy`, `accent`, `mist`, `surface.*`).
- **Do not introduce new UI/icon libraries** unless explicitly requested.

## Guardrails

- Ask before structural or visual changes.
- Contact form posts to a Google Apps Script webhook (`src/lib/contact.ts`), not
  Supabase — `src/lib/supabase.ts` is currently unused. Don't assume DB writes.
- Client env vars must be prefixed `VITE_`; never commit secrets (use Vercel env).
- Run `npm run lint` and `npm run typecheck` before finishing (`build` does not
  type-check).
- Update [`TASKS.md`](../../TASKS.md) after making changes.
